<!-- THE LAUNCHER ICON (the manifest's android:icon; the launcher and the
     recents card). Its picture (architect 2026-11-01, M7: Breeze only,
     everywhere; the project's quaver of 2026-10-23 retired 2026-11-02):
     BREEZE'S NOTE, assets/icons/AppIcon.svg (a symlink to
     MusicNote16th.svg, the logo lane's note, a `currentColor` drawing on a
     22 x 22 viewBox), rendered by resvg at the art's height in the
     `default` theme's text tone #B3B4BD (apk/build_apk.sh's LAUNCHER_INK,
     given as resvg's user stylesheet) and centered over THE APP'S GROUND,
     FLAT: #1F2128 (architect 2026-11-02: the icon wears the window's own
     ground — the `default` theme's whatever theme the window runs,
     2026-11-05; since 2026-11-12, session 114, SB Gunmetal_mod: "Gunmetal
     as the default, yes"; both READ by apk/build_apk.sh from
     themes/system/sb_gunmetal_mod.theme's SurfaceArea and
     ControlForeground lines, that file the one owner),
     one color over the whole
     canvas, so the mask shows a dark shape carrying the note. An
     ADAPTIVE icon, the whole of it: minSdk is 30, so
     no legacy ic_launcher.png set exists beside it.

     Two layers per density under res/mipmap-<density>/, BOTH RENDERED AT
     EVERY BUILD by apk/build_apk.sh's launcher step into its staged
     copy of res/:
       ic_launcher_background.png  the full 108 dp canvas flat in #1F2128;
       ic_launcher_foreground.png  the drawing rendered 52 dp tall, its width
                                   the viewBox's (52 dp: the note's viewBox
                                   is square), centred on a transparent
                                   canvas of the density's full 108 dp.

     THE 66 dp SAFE ZONE: an adaptive foreground's art should sit inside the
     mask's guaranteed-visible inner circle, Android's own 66 dp of the 108 dp
     canvas. The art 52 dp tall (architect 2026-10-16, his pick off a 60 /
     56 / 52 / 48 / 44 / 40 dp series on the glass: at 64 dp the art filled
     ~86 % of the launcher's visible tile and nearly touched its corners):
     the note's 22-unit viewBox at 52 / 22 = 2.36 dp a unit. Its ink spans
     x 6 .. 16 and y 3 .. 19 units (23.6 x 37.8 dp, measured off the path
     data); its farthest ink (the head's lower left, the ellipse about
     (9, 16.5) with radii 3 x 2.5) lies about 8.4 units, 19.9 dp, from the
     viewBox's center (11, 11), inside the 33 dp circle with about 13 dp to
     spare. The same 52 dp at every density (the per-density PNG pixel size
     scales with the density factor f alone):

       density  f    canvas C=108f  art 52f  offset (C-52f)/2
       mdpi     1    108            52       28
       hdpi     1.5  162            78       42
       xhdpi    2    216            104      56
       xxhdpi   3    324            156      84
       xxxhdpi  4    432            208      112

     A BUILD PRODUCT, NEVER COMMITTED: this file is the one tracked file of
     res/, and build_apk.sh writes the PNGs beside it in the package tree
     (byte-stable, -strip) from assets/icons/AppIcon.svg, Breeze's note, at
     the build. The safe-zone figure above is the note's. -->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background"/>
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground"/>
</adaptive-icon>
